00:08:48.215 --> 00:08:49.970
- AB InBev is one of
the largest brewing

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.390
companies in the entire world.

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.200
The key brands that we produce
are Budweiser, Bud Light,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.370
and Stella Artois.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.867
- Brewing is such
an old industry.

00:08:56.867 --> 00:08:59.450
And we've used a lot of the same
technologies for the last 100

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.030
years.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.613
And so we've started
to use technology

00:09:01.613 --> 00:09:03.320
to digitally transform
our operations.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:06.200
- Our innovation team at AB
InBev teams up with Google

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:09.320
and Pluto7 to find a way
to extend the life of each

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.520
K-Filter run, which is a process
where the beer has certain

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.550
particles that come
from fermentation,

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.650
and you have these filters that
are set up in which the beer

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:21.515
turbidity level, which
is how clear the beer is,

00:09:21.515 --> 00:09:23.580
has to get below a
certain threshold.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.780
So what you have is a multi
variable problem where when you

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:30.000
reach a certain threshold, the
machine has to be shut down.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.760
It's a balancing
act because you have

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:34.880
to keep that turbidity
level below the required

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.290
amount for that brand.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:39.020
- The K-Filter process is a very
manual process traditionally.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.187
What we've done is take a
lot of the human error out

00:09:41.187 --> 00:09:43.898
of that and automate and really
accelerate the decision making.

00:09:43.898 --> 00:09:46.190
- The solution was to take
this Google Machine Learning

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:49.100
Engine, put in billions
of simulations,

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.110
look for trends
within that data for,

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.330
this can prolong the
life here, or there.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.770
Not only does it
allow you longer

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.840
average runs but
there's energy savings,

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:58.920
and finally, there's
the beer itself,

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:02.060
which more uptime means you
can produce more as well as not

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.830
having to throw
out wasted brands.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:06.347
- The value of working in
the partnership with Pluto7

00:10:06.347 --> 00:10:08.930
is that they're scalable because
of the Google Cloud Platform.

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.388
So the learnings
we get from Newark

00:10:10.388 --> 00:10:13.070
we can scale across breweries
across 126 countries.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:15.440
And artificial intelligence
Pluto7 and Google Cloud

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.148
platform is a part of
this broader vision

00:10:17.148 --> 00:10:19.030
to transform how we make
beer, and deliver it

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:20.780
faster in more
consistently higher quality

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.040
to our valued customer.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.650
- Every opportunity we
have to be at the forefront

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:27.530
puts us in a position to
compete better, but also

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:29.870
prove that technology
like this can

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.751
be successful on an
industrial environment.

