00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:21.110
will show how you can--

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:24.010
for example, if temperature
is one of the variables,

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:26.260
and temperature is
one of the variables

00:23:26.260 --> 00:23:29.440
that matter in a
brewing process,

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:34.120
how you can monitor it
and proactively predict

00:23:34.120 --> 00:23:37.250
failures that could
impact the temperature.

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:41.020
So this is a single variable
solution that we have--

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:44.630
like I said, the full solution,
including the entire work

00:23:44.630 --> 00:23:48.127
that was done by our team,
will be available in AI Hub.

00:23:48.127 --> 00:23:50.460
And that's what I want to
quickly walk you guys through.

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:58.210
So before I go into the
details of the solution,

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:00.600
here is the visual.

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:02.370
What this shows you is--

00:24:02.370 --> 00:24:05.530
it will look at
how, in this case,

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:07.650
the temperature control
at the end of the day

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:11.610
is dependent on
basically two things, how

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:16.280
you put the heat back
in the controlled area,

00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:18.720
or you take heat out
of the controlled area,

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:20.820
and that is dependent
on basically

00:24:20.820 --> 00:24:23.460
the ambient temperature,
as it is noted.

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:26.910
So the machinery
that controls this,

00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:31.020
either you are having a heat
exchanger taking heat out,

00:24:31.020 --> 00:24:33.240
or you are having
a fan blower system

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:36.540
that is in a heating element
that is putting heat back in.

00:24:36.540 --> 00:24:40.260
So what this shows
actually is that--

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:45.855
how you can use data from
past and use that to predict

00:24:45.855 --> 00:24:48.190
when the failures will happen.

00:24:48.190 --> 00:24:50.890
And then you can put
in safety controls,

00:24:50.890 --> 00:24:54.540
so that before your temperature
variation becomes too much,

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:56.220
you can actually
take care of it.

00:24:56.220 --> 00:24:59.910
Or in this situation, if there
is a particular fan blower

00:24:59.910 --> 00:25:02.520
part that, for
example, will fail,

00:25:02.520 --> 00:25:04.290
you can know about
it in advance,

00:25:04.290 --> 00:25:08.100
so that you can take care of
it before it actually happens.

