So what I'm going to showcase
to you is, in this solution,

00:26:14.790 --> 00:26:18.480
what we have done is we
take this entire process

00:26:18.480 --> 00:26:22.740
of making sure that data,
which is your existing data,

00:26:22.740 --> 00:26:25.620
and you are continuously taking
additional data, because that's

00:26:25.620 --> 00:26:27.070
what you have to do--

00:26:27.070 --> 00:26:30.390
you're using that data
to make the model learn.

00:26:30.390 --> 00:26:33.290
So first of all, taking
the data, processing it,

00:26:33.290 --> 00:26:36.590
you are to use that
to train the model,

00:26:36.590 --> 00:26:40.590
you will do the evaluation,
and then deploy the new model,

00:26:40.590 --> 00:26:42.360
and then use it to
make prediction.

00:26:42.360 --> 00:26:47.670
So all of these steps that
I described, we actually--

00:26:47.670 --> 00:26:50.190
some of it is what
I'm showing you.

00:26:50.190 --> 00:26:53.520
As some people who are dealing
with either data science

00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:56.047
or machine learning, this
will be very familiar.

00:26:56.047 --> 00:26:57.630
The first part is
making sure that you

00:26:57.630 --> 00:26:59.640
have all the libraries loaded.

00:26:59.640 --> 00:27:02.640
Then you are preparing
the Google Storage

00:27:02.640 --> 00:27:05.200
to receive the
data that you need.

00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:08.490
And then we take
that data, make sure

00:27:08.490 --> 00:27:11.290
that the data
pre-processing is done.

00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:16.470
Then we take that data, and
now we are invoking the model.

00:27:16.470 --> 00:27:19.410
And the model is
then being trained.

00:27:19.410 --> 00:27:22.690
And after the training,
we do the evaluation.

00:27:22.690 --> 00:27:25.030
And after the
evaluation is done,

00:27:25.030 --> 00:27:29.940
we then deploy the model
back onto the GCM LE.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:32.020
And so this entire process--

00:27:32.020 --> 00:27:33.900
I'm just showing you a snippet.

00:27:33.900 --> 00:27:35.980
This whole thing is
like a Docker image.

00:27:35.980 --> 00:27:37.830
And there's a series
of Docker images

00:27:37.830 --> 00:27:40.440
that forms part of
the Kubleflow, which

00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:42.150
I'm going to talk
about and show you

00:27:42.150 --> 00:27:44.370
the architectural result next.

00:27:44.370 --> 00:27:48.250
And I mentioned the
fact that we are

00:27:48.250 --> 00:27:50.040
going to put the entire
solution that will

00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:52.390
be available to all of you.

00:27:52.390 --> 00:27:54.520
This is, not only are
we putting the solution,

00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:59.080
we are going to give
step by step instructions

00:27:59.080 --> 00:28:02.290
on how you can use
this genetic solution.

00:28:02.290 --> 00:28:07.120
And if you just take this
in a guide and go through it

00:28:07.120 --> 00:28:09.790
step by step, you can
actually take our solution

00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:13.390
