00:29:43.260 --> 00:29:46.050
The steps that you did
around developing the model.

00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:50.060
And now you do this with
a series of Kubeflows,

00:29:50.060 --> 00:29:53.300
and you keep deploying
it in multiple locations,

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:56.720
or you keep deploying
iterations of the model

00:29:56.720 --> 00:30:01.490
as new and newer models
are trained and evaluated

00:30:01.490 --> 00:30:03.312
to do the prediction.

00:30:09.310 --> 00:30:10.910
This is a generic slide.

00:30:10.910 --> 00:30:13.100
This basically
shows the advantage

00:30:13.100 --> 00:30:18.680
of using Kubeflow versus
how we had to do it before.

00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:21.770
What you have to do if you don't
use Kubeflow is go through all

00:30:21.770 --> 00:30:26.150
of the series of steps, and then
every time you have to deploy,

00:30:26.150 --> 00:30:28.355
you still need the
experts, who are

00:30:28.355 --> 00:30:31.490
the data scientist and
the data engineers,

00:30:31.490 --> 00:30:33.710
doing the steps in the red.

00:30:33.710 --> 00:30:37.010
So now the advantage is, once
the whole solution is actually

00:30:37.010 --> 00:30:40.850
done, all we need is basically
just a software engineer who

00:30:40.850 --> 00:30:45.890
can use Kubeflow and
deploy it without invoking

00:30:45.890 --> 00:30:48.590
the time of the data scientist
or the data engineer.

00:30:51.880 --> 00:30:53.800
This is just a visual.

00:30:53.800 --> 00:30:55.840
For those of you who are
already using Kubeflow,

00:30:55.840 --> 00:30:57.130
this will be familiar.

00:30:57.130 --> 00:30:58.900
The bottom line, think
about it this way,

00:30:58.900 --> 00:31:02.290
in a very simplistic manner,
Kubeflow is nothing but--

00:31:02.290 --> 00:31:06.220
if I were to simplify it,
you set up a cluster once,

00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:10.980
that's a one time setup,
that cluster using GKE

00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:14.670
is what you use then to
keep deploying pipelines,

00:31:14.670 --> 00:31:17.220
and these pipelines are
nothing but Docker containers

00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:21.510
where your set of either
solution or machine learning

00:31:21.510 --> 00:31:25.830
algorithms are containerized
and then deployed, so that it

00:31:25.830 --> 00:31:27.890
becomes a seamless deployment.

00:31:27.890 --> 00:31:29.550
So you can start with
a master and then

00:31:29.550 --> 00:31:32.010
you can have
multiple deployments

00:31:32.010 --> 00:31:34.570
in multiple locations
as required.

00:31:34.570 --> 00:31:37.520
A lot of you who are
working with Kubeflow

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:38.270
already know this.

00:31:38.270 --> 00:31:41.190
So, again, I'm not going to
go through that detail here.

00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:46.180
But my team is available if you
