00:36:53.290 --> 00:36:55.150
Don't worry about the buzzword.

00:36:55.150 --> 00:36:58.240
More important is, what
does it represent, right?

00:36:58.240 --> 00:37:03.340
So to simplify it, these
had three generations

00:37:03.340 --> 00:37:08.170
of key changes that changed
the way manufacturing was done.

00:37:08.170 --> 00:37:10.960
First was the invention
of the steam engine

00:37:10.960 --> 00:37:16.010
and the steam power that led
to the first manufacturing

00:37:16.010 --> 00:37:17.110
evolution.

00:37:17.110 --> 00:37:20.350
Then the whole concept of
mass production that was

00:37:20.350 --> 00:37:23.500
pioneered by Henry
Ford, that raised--

00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:27.250
basically improved the cost
and made a lot of the products

00:37:27.250 --> 00:37:29.240
accessible to the consumer.

00:37:29.240 --> 00:37:33.250
Then we had the
computer-aided innovation.

00:37:33.250 --> 00:37:36.880
And now finally, with
AI, cloud computing,

00:37:36.880 --> 00:37:40.750
and IOT coming together
we are on the cusp

00:37:40.750 --> 00:37:44.760
of the next great innovation
around manufacturing, which you

00:37:44.760 --> 00:37:47.050
will hear is Manufacturing 4.0.

00:37:47.050 --> 00:37:48.470
That's what it is.

00:37:48.470 --> 00:37:51.310
